From 3cc3f73886d26c78579aec5f39dcaebe74c7d9d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ed <edimoldovan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:17:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 25/31] phy: apple: t6050-usb2: SuperSpeed glue, logging and
 test switches

The SuperSpeed sequence on J714c port 1 trains the link on some boots
only. This commit carries what the boots since 16b3737ba9a7 used:

- The iBoot glue values (cd28/cd2c 0x886, cd40 0x3c20060c, cd44
  0x2000b) are written before step 1. phy_calibrate() writes them back
  after the xHCI reset where they differ, instead of the snapshot taken
  at step 16 (the glue reads 0 while CIO is on, so the snapshot was 0).
- cd28 is logged after each step; a 3 s work after the xHCI reset logs
  every change of both PORTSC registers and GDBGLTSSM.
- The PHY CPU boot drains for its full second after AP and IOP power on
  and sends IOP power after 3 s even without the AP ack.
- Boot parameters: ss_pace_us (gap after each sequence write, default
  0), ss_settle_ms (pause after step 16, default 0), ss_susphy (set
  GUSB3PIPECTL SUSPHY before step 1, default 1).

Checked on J714c: without pacing and SUSPHY, 3 of 8 boots at
SuperSpeed Plus; with 1 ms pacing 0 of 8; with a 2 s settle 0 of 4;
with SUSPHY 0 of 4 (the SS port then trains late, after the USB 2.0
enumeration, and falls to SS.Inactive).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8a35cd889cff3f12e3361d96fe8dc825cc2b7c2f)
